      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Withrow_Park"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The park honors John Jacob Withrow, a 19th‑century builder and city alderman who helped found the Canadian National Exhibition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Withrow_Park"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In February 2008, the Toronto Maple Leafs practiced on Withrow Park’s newly refurbished outdoor ice rink, drawing national attention.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Withrow_Park"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every Saturday, the park hosts a bustling farmer’s market that showcases local produce and crafts for the Riverdale community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://torontoforyou.com/withrow-park-riverdale-features-programs-events-more/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Withrow Park’s boundaries are Carlaw Avenue to the east, Bain Avenue to the south, Logan Avenue to the west, and McConnell Avenue to the north.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
